{"name":"Foggy Sunrise","hex":"#a79c8e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"foggy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Obscured by mist or fog; unclear; hazy.","Confused, befuddled, or vague."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foggy"},{"term":"sunrise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time of day when the sun appears above the eastern horizon.","The change in color of the sky at dawn."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To phase in.","To awake."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunrise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fog","blocks":[{"text":"Fog is a visible aerosol consisting of tiny water droplets or ice crystals held in the air near the Earth's surface. Fog can be considered a type of low-lying cloud usually resembling stratus and is heavily influenced by nearby bodies of water, topography, and wind conditions. In turn, fog affects many human activities, such as shipping, travel, and warfare. Recent atmospheric research indicates that fog also functions as an active aquatic ecosystem. Fog droplets harbor microbiomes where bacteria actively grow, divide, and interact with atmospheric chemistry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg/330px-A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fog"},{"title":"Sunrise","blocks":[{"text":"Sunrise is the moment when the upper rim of the Sun appears on the horizon in the morning, at the start of the Sun path. The term can also refer to the entire process of the solar disk crossing the horizon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg/330px-Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunrise"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wiki